    {
      "name": "HDD 6TB",
      "description": "The 6TB, read out of /sys by the agent on jug2. Both boards boot from their SSD, so a dead SSD is a dead board and the ping already says so. This is the only disk that can vanish without anything else noticing. Sysfs rather than the mount table: a disconnected disk leaves its mount entry behind and a mount-based check sits green over a drive that is physically gone.",
